To obtain an informed initialization of the assignments between offensive and defensive players at the beginning of each play, we adopt a probabilistic matching approach based on the vertical distances between players. Specifically, for each defender \( i \) and each of the \( N = 5 \) potential offensive players \( j \), we compute a similarity score using a softmax over the negative distances,
\[
\delta_{ij} = \frac{\exp(-\alpha \, |\mathrm{y}^{(\text{def})}_i - \mathrm{y}^{(\text{att})}_j|)}{\sum_{k=1}^{n_{\text{att}}} \exp(-\alpha \, |\mathrm{y}^{(\text{def})}_i - \mathrm{y}^{(\text{att})}_k|)} \, ,
\]

\begin{align*}
\Embedding_{0} & =
\begin{bmatrix}
f_{\gamecontext}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\gamecontext}\right) & f_{\game}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\game}\right) \\ f_{\teamstrength}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\teamstrength}\right) & f_{\team}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\team}\right) \\ f_{\playerstrength}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\playerstrength}\right) & f_{\player}\left(\matr{X}^{(n)}_{\player}\right)
\end{bmatrix} \\
& \in \Reals^{H \times W \times D}\text{, where } H = P^{(n)} + 2 + 1 \text{, and } W =  T^{(n)} + 1 \text{.}
